WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.630
Earth has become an urban planet.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.260
Cities are growing everywhere.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.440
More than half of the world’s people

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.620
already live in cities.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.719
By 2050, 2 out of 3 of us will live in a city.

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:15.679
That has sobering implications for the environment.

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:17.279
Cities consume vast amounts of

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.560
food, energy, and materials.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.720
This “ecological footprint” can extend

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.760
far beyond the city’s edge.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.620
Indeed, the land area needed to support a city

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:31.200
can be 200 times bigger than the area of the city itself.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.100
Another challenge is that cities are expanding into areas

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.720
rich in biodiversity.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.200
That’s because we like to live in the same places

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.020
that are favored by plants and animals.

00:00:41.359 --> 00:00:43.929
Cities alter the environment in dramatic ways.

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:45.760
Tons of concrete store heat...

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.360
City centers become “heat islands” that are

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.800
warmer at night and hotter by day.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.500
Urban are noisy… and artificial light means

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.840
it never gets really dark.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.870
Paved roads and rooftops prevent water

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.820
from soaking into the soil.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.729
That leads to flash floods and lots of polluted runoff

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:08.100
that can harms streams and rivers.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:11.500
But an urban planet is not all gloom and doom.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.820
When you put a lot of people in one place,

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.100
you can improve efficiency.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.040
City dwellers can use a lot less energy, per person,

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.540
than people living in rural areas.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.780
Doing it right will require smart planning.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.140
And one thing is clear:

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:30.270
Cities are here to stay, and the decisions we make today

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.590
about how we build and live in them

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.180
will shape generations to come.

